'   none; its index entry is removed)
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.
'
' ── STATUS (2026-10-17): DONE (wt) ─────────────────────────────────────────
' DECIDED by the user on 2026-10-16 (TUI; D1–D9 below); this spec was written
' first as the goal, and the code has landed in the working tree
' (repo-simplification.puml D2 → DONE (wt)). Everything below is MEASURED by
' reading the tree unless marked. The coordinator reports, measured on this
' VM: unit tests green except the known TestJVMRowNeedsTheQemuFloorOnMacOSHosts;
' vet clean for every tag plus darwin and windows; golangci unused 0;
' TestImageOpencode green on a freshly built proveo/opencode:local;
' test_opencode_runtime.py OK; the e2e package green except the known
' TestScheduleAgentThatDiesBeforeReadyFailsFast. [Unverified] here: the sbx
' legs — no sbx on that VM.
' 2026-10-20: the import streams the database over `sbx exec -i` stdin; it no
' longer stages through `sbx cp` (WHY STDIN, NOT `sbx cp` below).
'
' ── THE DECISIONS (the user, 2026-10-16; verbatim TUI labels where given) ───
' The architect's brief recommended an option for each; where the user chose
' differently, the user's answer is what this spec records.
'   D1 "Carry the DB over" — when an engine's settings change (the image after
'      `mise run build`, the kit, the mounts) and it is replaced, its database is
'      copied to the host and imported into the new engine. (The architect had
'      recommended never retiring without a headed yes.)
'   D2 `--shell`: "if `proveo` retire it" — retired 2026-10-17. A shell in the
'      engine is sbx's: `sbx exec -it <engine> bash`.
'   D3 keep injecting `--standalone` (and `--auto` for headless `run`).
'   D4 "Let OpenCode handle it" — no proveo lock on concurrent launches.
'   D5 an import failure removes the fresh engine and its receipt, stops the
'      run, and the next run retries.
'   D6 every new engine imports once.
'   D7 engines created before this change retire like any sandbox; their
'      history sits in the V2 share and the import restores it; the legacy
'      owner record is deleted.
'   D8 "Accept and document" — in-engine logins persist until `sbx rm`.
'   D9 this spec, then delete the plan after rehoming the facts that still
'      matter (REHOMED below).
'
' ── WHERE THE DATABASE LIVES ───────────────────────────────────────────────
' OpenCode's native default: $HOME/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db, with HOME
' = /home/agent in sbx. proveo sets neither OPENCODE_DB nor XDG_DATA_HOME for an
' agent launch. The engine scripts resolve the path the way OpenCode does
' (opencode_history.go openCodeDatabasePath): OPENCODE_DB, else
' $XDG_DATA_HOME/opencode/opencode.db, else ~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db.
' The file is on the engine's own disk; it survives reattach and `sbx stop` and
' goes with `sbx rm` (REHOMED, sbx persistence). proveo never writes it back to
' the host: entrypoint-lib.sh skips .local/share/opencode in both sync loops
' (:2568, :2661). defs/opencode/harness.manifest maps only opencode/v2/config
' (the V2 share mount is gone), and TestOpenCodeHomeAccessMountsConfigButNeverHistory
' (home_access_test.go) pins that against the real manifest: none of
' opencode/v2/share, opencode/share, .local/share/opencode or opencode/carry is
' mounted.
'
' ── A NEW ENGINE IMPORTS ONCE (opencode_engine.go ensureOpenCodeEngine; D6) ─
' Run calls it for opencode and opencode-browser (opencodeTarget), and again in
' the template-reload retry; its `created` result is what sets in.CloneKnown.
'   0. An existing engine → sbx.Reattach, no create, no import.
'   1. `sbx create` (createOpenCodeEngine), not `sbx run`: the import must
'      finish before the agent's first open, and `sbx run` starts the agent.
'   2. openCodeImportSource: the FIRST REGULAR FILE (os.Lstat; a symlink is
'      skipped) of, under the proveo home:
'        opencode/carry/<engine>.db         (the D1 carry)
'        opencode/v2/share/opencode.db      (the V2 share)
'        opencode/share/opencode.db         (the pre-V2 share)
'        .local/share/opencode/opencode.db
'      None → "OpenCode: new engine <name> starts with empty history".
'   3. importOpenCodeHistory stats the db and any -wal / -journal
'      (sbx.OpenCodeImportFiles), starts `sbx exec -i -w / <engine> -- python3
'      -I -c OpenCodeImportScript` (OpenCodeImportArgs) and writes its stdin
'      with sbx.WriteOpenCodeImport: a tar of one member per file
'      (opencode.db, opencode.db-wal, opencode.db-journal), then an empty
'      `commit` member (OpenCodeImportCommit) — written only when a re-stat
'      finds every file unchanged. A size or mtime change, or a side appearing
'      or vanishing, withholds the commit and fails with "<src> changed while
'      it was copied; close the OpenCode that writes it". It never sends -shm,
'      never writes the source, and names no path inside the engine.
'   4. The script: exit 3 at once if the engine already has a database
'      (accepted as done; it reads no stdin); else `mkdtemp` a private dir it
'      owns and extract only the three known member names into it. No commit
'      member, a cut stream or an unknown member → exit 5
'      (OpenCodeImportIncomplete), nothing installed. Then `PRAGMA
'      quick_check` (exit 4 → "<src> fails SQLite's quick_check"), fold the
'      WAL through SQLite's backup API into a temp file BESIDE the target,
'      chmod 0600, `link()` it into place — never over an existing file — and
'      remove the private dir on every path. Exit 0 = imported.
'   5. A consumed carry file is deleted ("OpenCode: carried history (<size>)
'      into new engine <name>"); a share source prints "OpenCode: imported <src>
'      (<size>) into new engine <name> once; the host copy stays unchanged".
'      The host V2 share is NEVER edited.
'   6. Run reattaches with `sbx run --name <engine>`.
' D5: any other failure (change, exec, incomplete stream, corrupt) `sbx rm`s
' the fresh engine, deletes its receipt and stops the run: "OpenCode history
' import into <engine> failed: … — the new engine was removed and <src> stays;
' the next run retries".
'
' ── WHY STDIN, NOT `sbx cp` (2026-10-20) ───────────────────────────────────
' REPORTED: TestOpenCodeEngineKeepsHistoryAndImportsOnce failed on a macOS
' host. The import (uid 1000 under `sbx exec`) raised PermissionError [Errno
' 13] on shutil.copyfile of /tmp/proveo-import-opencode.db, then [Errno 1] on
' os.unlink of it. `sbx cp` had left the stage owned by another uid with the
' source's 0600 mode (carryOpenCodeHistory always writes 0600), and /tmp is
' sticky, so uid 1000 could neither read nor remove it.
' MEASURED 2026-10-20 in a python:3.12-slim stand-in: a root-owned 0600 file in
' /tmp gives uid 1000 exactly those two errors.
' The sbx cp reference documents no ownership or mode rule
' (https://docs.docker.com/reference/cli/sbx/cp/, read 2026-10-20).
' docker cp: "files copied to a container are created with UID:GID of the root
' user", permissions "preserved if possible"
' (https://docs.docker.com/reference/cli/docker/container/cp/, read
' 2026-10-20). [Inference] sbx cp follows that rule; the failure fits it.
' The sbx exec reference documents "-i, --interactive Keep STDIN open even if
' not attached" and "Flags match the behavior of docker exec"
' (https://docs.docker.com/reference/cli/sbx/exec/, read 2026-10-20).
' So the bytes travel on stdin into a dir the engine user creates: nothing in
' the engine is owned by anyone else, and no fixed /tmp path exists to collide.
' The commit member keeps the change verdict in-band: the host re-stats after
' the bytes leave and before the engine installs, within one exec.
' The script reads stdin unbuffered (sys.stdin.buffer.raw), so it acts on the
' commit member without waiting for EOF.
' NOT TAKEN: `sbx exec -u root … chown 1000:1000` + chmod on a unique stage
' path — two more execs, and the engine still holds a root-written file.
'
' ── A REPLACED ENGINE CARRIES ITS DATABASE (D1, D7) ────────────────────────
' retireSandbox (launch_receipt.go), for an OpenCode engine, runs
' carryOpenCodeHistory AFTER PreserveClone and BEFORE SaveState and `sbx rm`:
' `sbx exec -w / <engine> -- python3 -I -c OpenCodeExportScript` opens the
' engine database with a 30 s busy timeout, takes a backup-API single-file copy,
' switches the copy to DELETE journal mode and streams it on stdout. The host
' writes <home>/opencode/carry/<engine>.db.partial (0600), checks the SQLite
' header (OpenCodeDatabaseHeader), renames it to .db and prints "OpenCode:
' carried <engine>'s history (<size>) to <path> for the engine that replaces
' it"; the .partial is removed on every path.
'   exit 3 (OpenCodeExportNone) → no database at the native path, i.e. a legacy
'     keeper engine (D7: its history lived in a /tmp cache) → nothing carried;
'     the new engine imports from the V2 share.
'   any other failure → retire refuses and the engine is kept: "OpenCode
'     history could not be carried out of <engine> (…) — it is kept;
'     `sbx rm --force <engine>` deletes it with its history".
' After the rm, retireSandbox deletes the receipt and the legacy owner record
' (<receipt dir>/<engine>.opencode-cache.json, legacyOwnerRecord). The
' opencode-only "engine is running" refusal in retireIfStale is gone: OpenCode
' follows the generic stale-sandbox rule (kit-lifecycle.puml). The headed
' prompt (choiceui.SandboxUpgradeCopy, now the only prompt in blocked_run.go)
' adds "Its OpenCode history moves to the new sandbox."
'
' ── RETENTION AND REMOVAL ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
' A normal end keeps the engine (normalEndOf → endRetainEngine) and prints
' "OpenCode: history lives in retained engine <name>; `sbx rm --force <name>`
' deletes it" (sandbox.go Run) — e2e/seed_ready_test.go matches "retained
' engine ". `sbx rm` deletes the engine and its history, and so does the
' Ctrl+C "remove" answer; no carry runs on either.
'
' ── THE IMAGE SIDE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' packages/lib/proveo-opencode-runtime is a 103-line THIN WRAPPER, keeping its
' name so the image shim (Dockerfile:93) stays:
'   * native_command injects `--auto` before `--` for headless `run`, and
'     `--standalone` for state commands unless `--server` is given (D3);
'   * the git-sync commit-subject helper (PROVEO_GIT_SYNC_MSG_INFLIGHT=1) and
'     diagnostics (--version/-v/--help/-h/--completions before `--`) run with
'     their args UNCHANGED in a throwaway dir: its own XDG_DATA_HOME,
'     XDG_STATE_HOME, OPENCODE_DB and TMPDIR, a copy of the config with
'     service.json {"disabled": true}, signals forwarded, the dir removed;
'   * everything else is os.execv of the native client.
'   `debug …` is no longer treated as a diagnostic: it runs against the engine
'   database (reported; MEASURED that diagnostic() lists only the flags above).
' The image no longer gates the seed: proveo-seed and defs/opencode/entrypoint.sh
' carry no prepared-history check, proveo-await-seed stops only on a seed
' refusal (TestAwaitSeedStopsOnlyOnASeedRefusal), and proveo_opencode_sync_data
' is gone from entrypoint-lib.sh. The Dockerfile ENTRYPOINT is
' ["dumb-init","--","/entrypoint.sh"] and its python check is
' `python3 -c 'import sqlite3'`.
' DELETED (MEASURED absent): packages/lib/opencode_cache.py,
' opencode-credentials.py, proveo-opencode-preflight, opencode_startup.py,
' test_opencode_credentials.py, test_opencode_runtime_native.py,
' opencode-runtime-fixture.py, opencode-truncation-driver.mjs, and every
' tracked OpenCode .pyc under packages/lib/__pycache__; internal/backend/
' sandbox/opencode_cache.go, opencode_cache_test.go and
' opencode_history_image_test.go; e2e/opencode_prepared_history_test.go and
' e2e/opencode_cache_sbx_test.go (rewritten as opencode_engine_sbx_test.go). The
' reset/prepare/recovery prompts left internal/choiceui. headedConfirm,
' agentTerminal and openScreen moved unchanged to internal/backend/sandbox/
' confirm.go. load_credentials and the Keeper went with opencode_cache.py, so
' the os.environ / Keeper-env split recorded before (repo-simplification.puml
' D2) is gone with them. test_opencode_startup.py is trimmed, not deleted.
'
' ── TESTS (MEASURED to exist; pass/fail as reported above) ─────────────────
'   internal/sbx/opencode_history_test.go — 6, each feeding the script the
'     stream sbx.WriteOpenCodeImport writes: import once and refuse a second;
'     refuse a corrupt copy; install nothing without the commit (no stdin,
'     cut before the commit, cut inside a file, an unknown member); withhold
'     the commit from a changing source (db grows, -wal grows, -journal
'     appears); export a consistent copy; argv shapes (`exec -i`, no path).
'     Each import case also checks its TMPDIR is left empty.
'   internal/backend/sandbox/opencode_engine_test.go (!windows) — a fake sbx
'     on PATH that runs the REAL scripts against a guest dir: an existing
'     engine is left alone (1); the import source order, the empty start and
'     the symlink skip (5); a failed import removes the fresh engine and keeps
'     the source — corrupt, changed mid-copy, exec failure (3); retire carries
'     the history, carries nothing from an engine with none, keeps the engine
'     when the export fails (3). 12 cases by count (the brief said 11).
'     The fake hands the script stdin only under `exec -i`, fails any `sbx
'     cp`, and runs it with TMPDIR=<guest>/tmp; an import must leave that
'     empty and log `exec -i`. Each failure case names its error; the
'     mid-stream change uses a 4 MiB source, so the host blocks on the pipe
'     until the fake has grown it.
'   internal/backend/sandbox/home_access_test.go
'     TestOpenCodeHomeAccessMountsConfigButNeverHistory.
'   internal/imagetest/opencode_test.go ocHistory — 3 checks in the image: two
'     shim launches share the native default database and create no V2 share
'     and leave no throwaway dir; the inflight call leaves the engine database
'     byte-identical; "uid 1000 imports a root-staged 0600 WAL stream once
'     and the export streams it": a root container builds the WAL fixture,
'     the host writes it 0600 and builds the stream with
'     sbx.WriteOpenCodeImport, and a second root container saves that stream
'     as a root-owned 0600 file, checks uid 1000 cannot read it, and hands it
'     as stdin to the import run as uid 1000 — installed 1000/0600, a second
'     import exits 3, no /tmp/proveo-import-* is left, the export carries the
'     SQLite header and both rows. MEASURED 2026-10-20 green on a
'     python:3.12-slim stand-in with a uid-1000 user; NOT run on
'     proveo/opencode (not built on that VM).
'   internal/contract/opencode_credentials_test.go TestOpenCodeRuntimeFixtures,
'     TestOpenCodeImageShipsOnlyTheThinRuntime, TestOpenCodeDocumentsEngineLocalLogins;
'     e2e/opencode_credentials_test.go TestOpenCodeRuntimeInImage.
'   e2e/opencode_engine_sbx_test.go TestOpenCodeEngineKeepsHistoryAndImportsOnce:
'     the first run prints "imported <share>/opencode.db"; api POST; reattach
'     GET; `sbx stop` then GET; the host share stays byte-identical; then a
'     `docker tag` retag of the image forces a replacement whose run prints
'     "carried <engine>'s history" and "carried history" and reads the same
'     session. [Unverified]: not run — no sbx on the verifying VM.
'
' ── REHOMED FROM THE DELETED PLAN (D9) ─────────────────────────────────────
' SBX PERSISTENCE AND REMOVAL (docs read 2026-10-14, quoted then):
'   https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/architecture/ : everything inside a
'     sandbox "persists until you remove it", "agent state and history"
'     included; `sbx rm` deletes "all of its contents".
'   https://github.com/docker/sbx-releases/releases v0.42.0: a new sandbox
'     reusing a deleted name "no longer inherits its files, Docker images, or
'     agent session history".
'   "By default, a local sandbox stops automatically shortly after its last
'     session disconnects" (https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/customize/
'     author/; 30 s grace, docker/sbx-releases#452; `sbx create` sandboxes since
'     v0.43.0). "The rest of the VM filesystem persists across restarts"
'     (https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/security/isolation/); processes
'     and memory do not. That auto-stop is what killed the old in-memory
'     keeper ~30 s after every run; an on-disk database is unaffected.
' KIT LIMITS (https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/customize/kits-v2/, read
' 2026-10-14): startup commands "don't gate the agent's entrypoint"; "Use
' setup.files for any value that needs to land on disk before the agent runs";
' setup.files writes text content; a kit "can't read arbitrary host environment
' variables or files"; v2 volumes take no host source. So no kit surface can
' carry a SQLite database in — hence `sbx create` + `sbx exec -i` (the database
' on stdin) before the reattach. https://docs.docker.com/ai/sandboxes/agents/opencode/
' documents no data or history path and no import.
' SQLITE WAL ACROSS MACHINES:
'   * SQLite's active state stays on the ENGINE'S LOCAL filesystem, never a
'     database shared across VMs through a mount: WAL coordinates writers
'     through the -shm shared-memory index, which only works between
'     processes on one host ([Unverified] https://www.sqlite.org/wal.html).
'     Cross-VM file locking through sbx mounts was never measured.
'   * Every OpenCode 2.x database runs in WAL mode; a clean exit removes -wal
'     and -shm, and OpenCode writes the database on every open.
'   * SQLite cannot open a WAL database read-only in a directory where it
'     cannot create the -shm (measured 2026-10-15: "unable to open database
'     file"; [Unverified] https://www.sqlite.org/wal.html, "Read-Only
'     Databases"). So the import writes the streamed files into a private
'     writable temp dir and opens them there, and the host never sends a
'     -shm, which describes another machine's memory.
' E2E FACTS: an sbx e2e must keep the operator's HOME, where sbx keeps its
' login — with a temporary HOME `sbx template load` failed "Not authenticated
' to Docker" (2026-10-15); only PROVEO_HOME is temporary. [Inference] `sbx run`
' with no TTY and stdin at EOF does not return the agent's output, so e2e legs
' drive proveo on a pty. Each "[A]pprove all" saves a per-service binding in
' the operator's ~/.config/sbx/credentials.yaml, which outlives the test — so
' since SEC3 (2026-10-17) the e2e never approves: it fails naming the services
' and asks for one interactive `proveo run <target>` (_spec/tests/
' testing-strategy.puml).
'
' ── RISKS AND RESIDUALS, RECORDED ──────────────────────────────────────────
'   * D8: credentials live with the engine. V2 keeps tokens in SQLite beside
'     the sessions; an in-engine login persists until `sbx rm`, readable by
'     the agent's uid and by `sbx exec`, and proveo never moves it to the host
'     — except inside a D1 carry, which copies the whole database, logins
'     included, through <home>/opencode/carry. [Unverified] A legacy V1
'     database may carry credential rows into the import.
'   * `sbx rm` loses the history unless a carry ran first: the Ctrl+C remove,
'     an operator's `sbx rm`, and name reuse all lose it.
'   * Every engine in every workspace imports the same snapshot of the share,
'     and the copies diverge; nothing merges them back.
'   * The Dockerfile still copies defs/opencode/harness.manifest to
'     /usr/local/lib/proveo/opencode.harness.manifest (Dockerfile:80), and
'     nothing in the image reads it now (reported; a simplification candidate,
'     repo-simplification.puml).
'   * [Inference] The old preflight ENTRYPOINT waited up to 300 s for the
'     seed-done marker; that wait is gone with it.
'   * RESOLVED 2026-10-20 (was "[Unverified] `sbx cp` file ownership"): the
'     ownership broke the import for uid 1000; the import no longer uses
'     `sbx cp` (WHY STDIN, NOT `sbx cp`).
'   * [Unverified] `sbx exec -i` carrying a multi-MB binary stdin and its EOF
'     on a live engine — no sbx on the verifying VM; the e2e is the proof.
'   * [Unverified] sbx create's "Created sandbox" output on a live engine.
'   * [Unverified] OpenCode's behaviour with two clients on one SQLite
'     database (D4: no proveo lock; the old runtime refused a second client
'     with exit 75).
'   * The first launch on a new engine pays the copy (measured store sizes:
'     _spec/packages/lib/opencode-seed-progress.puml) plus OpenCode's own
'     migration; later launches do no proveo history work.
'   * The git-sync commit-subject helper runs on a throwaway database, so it
'     cannot use an in-engine OAuth login ([Inference]; it falls back to the
'     paths summary, _spec/packages/lib/git-sync-turn.puml).
'
' ── NON-GOALS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' No host-side store, publication, sanitizer, cross-engine sharing or merge.
' No backup or export command. No docker-backend path. No host-owned OAuth (it
' stays PLANNED). The host V2 share is never deleted or edited. Other
' harnesses retire as before.
title OpenCode engine-local history — import once, carry on replacement, keep until sbx rm

participant "proveo run opencode\n(host)" as PV <<app>>
database "proveo home\nopencode/carry · v2/share · share" as HOMEDB <<db>>
participant "sbx" as SBX <<cloud>>
participant "engine\n~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db" as ENG <<host>>
participant "opencode\nthin runtime → native" as OC <<app>>

group new engine (ensureOpenCodeEngine)
  PV ARROW_MAIN SBX : sbx create <engine>
  PV ARROW_OPTIONAL HOMEDB : first regular file:\ncarry/<engine>.db · v2/share · share · .local/share
  PV ARROW_MAIN ENG : sbx exec -i python3 -I -c OpenCodeImportScript\nstdin: tar db (+ -wal, -journal) · commit; never -shm
  ENG ARROW_MAIN ENG : extract into own mkdtemp · quick_check\nbackup API · link() only if absent · 0600
  alt exit 0, or 3 (already has one)
    PV ARROW_OPTIONAL HOMEDB : delete the consumed carry file
  else change / exec / incomplete / corrupt (D5)
    PV ARROW_ERROR SBX : sbx rm <engine>; receipt removed; run stops
  end
end
PV ARROW_MAIN SBX : sbx run --name <engine> (reattach)
SBX ARROW_MAIN OC : agent launch
OC ARROW_MAIN ENG : native default path; --auto / --standalone
PV ARROW_OPTIONAL PV : teardown keeps the engine:\n"history lives in retained engine <name>"

group settings changed (retireSandbox, D1 / D7)
  PV ARROW_MAIN ENG : sbx exec python3 -I -c OpenCodeExportScript
  ENG ARROW_MAIN PV : stdout: single-file copy (DELETE journal)
  PV ARROW_MAIN HOMEDB : carry/<engine>.db.partial → header check → .db (0600)
  alt exit 3: legacy keeper engine (D7)
    PV ARROW_OPTIONAL HOMEDB : nothing carried; the V2 share is the source
  else export failed
    PV ARROW_ERROR PV : retire refuses; the old engine is kept
  end
  PV ARROW_MAIN SBX : sbx rm --force <engine>; legacy owner record deleted
end

note over ENG
  **The engine owns the database.** proveo
  sets no OPENCODE_DB or XDG_DATA_HOME, so
  OpenCode opens its own default path, kept
  until ""sbx rm"".
end note

note right of PV
  **Import once, over stdin.** The host streams
  the source and commits only if it did not
  change; it never sends -shm or writes it.
end note

note over SBX
  **A failed import removes the new engine.**
  Its receipt goes too, the carry file stays,
  and the next run tries again.
end note

note right of HOMEDB
  **A replaced engine carries its database.**
  The export lands in opencode/carry, and the
  next new engine imports it first.
end note

note over OC
